# build output
dist/

# generated types
.astro/

# dependencies
node_modules/

# logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# environment variables
.env
.env.production

# macOS-specific files
.DS_Store
coverage/

# Both generated CVs are deliberately tracked: ctaform.astro links to /cv.pdf and
# /cv-onepage.pdf, and public/ is copied verbatim into the build, so an untracked file
# would 404 on the deployed site. (public/cv.pdf was listed here while still tracked,
# which had no effect but read as though the download were disposable.)

# Working CV drafts, kept locally only. Anchored to the repo root so this cannot match
# public/*.pdf — a bare *.pdf would silently stop the published downloads being tracked.
/*.pdf

# Byte-cache left behind whenever the .claude/ hooks or skill scripts are imported or
# syntax-checked. cv-only, because spotlite ships no Python.
__pycache__/

# The verbatim extraction of CHRISTIE.ARJ (a December 1992 floppy backup of a May 1990
# snapshot). 373 files of 1987 source, kept locally as the working copy and as the thing
# the project reconstructions were assembled from. What gets published is the four zips
# in public/, so this tree is deliberately untracked rather than committed twice.
/christie/
